<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_section">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1" title="In 6 Main Results ‣ Does the Judge Prefer English?Evaluating Language-Switching Invariance in LLM-as-a-Judge" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Accuracy is highest in English.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2" title="In 6 Main Results ‣ Does the Judge Prefer English?Evaluating Language-Switching Invariance in LLM-as-a-Judge" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Language transformations cause substantial preference flips.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3" title="In 6 Main Results ‣ Does the Judge Prefer English?Evaluating Language-Switching Invariance in LLM-as-a-Judge" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Correctness changes nearly as often as preferences.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S6.SS0.SSS0.Px4" title="In 6 Main Results ‣ Does the Judge Prefer English?Evaluating Language-Switching Invariance in LLM-as-a-Judge" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">No simple English preference in tie probes.</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_section"><a href="#S7" title="In Does the Judge Prefer English?Evaluating Language-Switching Invariance in LLM-as-a-Judge" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">7 </span>Extended Analysis</span></a>
<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_section">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S7.SS0.SSS0.Px1" title="In 7 Extended Analysis ‣ Does the Judge Prefer English?Evaluating Language-Switching Invariance in LLM-as-a-Judge" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Transformation audit supports a sensitivity check.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S7.SS0.SSS0.Px2" title="In 7 Extended Analysis ‣ Does the Judge Prefer English?Evaluating Language-Switching Invariance in LLM-as-a-Judge" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Subset averages reveal two distinct effects.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S7.SS0.SSS0.Px3" title="In 7 Extended Analysis ‣ Does the Judge Prefer English?Evaluating Language-Switching Invariance in LLM-as-a-Judge" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Chinese and language-switching are not identical perturbations.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S7.SS0.SSS0.Px4" title="In 7 Extended Analysis ‣ Does the Judge Prefer English?Evaluating Language-Switching Invariance in LLM-as-a-Judge" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Language-switching amplifies position sensitivity.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S7.SS0.SSS0.Px5" title="In 7 Extended Analysis ‣ Does the Judge Prefer English?Evaluating Language-Switching Invariance in LLM-as-a-Judge" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Adversarial subsets are harder and less invariant.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S7.SS0.SSS0.Px6" title="In 7 Extended Analysis ‣ Does the Judge Prefer English?Evaluating Language-Switching Invariance in LLM-as-a-Judge" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Model families differ in failure mode.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S7.SS0.SSS0.Px7" title="In 7 Extended Analysis ‣ Does the Judge Prefer English?Evaluating Language-Switching Invariance in LLM-as-a-Judge" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">The tie probe separates bias from instability.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S7.SS0.SSS0.Px8" title="In 7 Extended Analysis ‣ Does the Judge Prefer English?Evaluating Language-Switching Invariance in LLM-as-a-Judge" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Qualitative failure modes.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S7.SS0.SSS0.Px9" title="In 7 Extended Analysis ‣ Does the Judge Prefer English?Evaluating Language-Switching Invariance in LLM-as-a-Judge" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Reproducibility checks.</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_section"><a href="#S8" title="In Does the Judge Prefer English?Evaluating Language-Switching Invariance in LLM-as-a-Judge" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">8 </span>Recommended Workflow</span></a>
<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_section">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S8.SS0.SSS0.Px1" title="In 8 Recommended Workflow ‣ Does the Judge Prefer English?Evaluating Language-Switching Invariance in LLM-as-a-Judge" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Cost remains low.</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_section"><a href="#S9" title="In Does the Judge Prefer English?Evaluating Language-Switching Invariance in LLM-as-a-Judge" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref">9 </span>Discussion</span></a>
<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_section">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S9.SS0.SSS0.Px1" title="In 9 Discussion ‣ Does the Judge Prefer English?Evaluating Language-Switching Invariance in LLM-as-a-Judge" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Implication for multilingual evaluation.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S9.SS0.SSS0.Px2" title="In 9 Discussion ‣ Does the Judge Prefer English?Evaluating Language-Switching Invariance in LLM-as-a-Judge" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Implication for prompt design.</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_paragraph"><a href="#S9.SS0.SSS0.Px3" title="In 9 Discussion ‣ Does the Judge Prefer English?Evaluating Language-Switching Invariance in LLM-as-a-Judge" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title">Relation to robustness evaluation.</span></a></li>
